  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Iriskumaonin methyl ether may interact with HepG2 through multiple indirect pathways. The compound is identified as a target of Hepatocyte and Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which in turn targets (Z)-Pentadecenoic acid and 9-Methoxy-4-(methoxymethyl)-3,5-dimethylbenzo[f][1]benzofuran, respectively. These intermediates ultimately have a target of HepG2, indicating a potential downstream effect of Iriskumaonin methyl ether on the HepG2 cell line. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with varying degrees of support from different molecular mechanisms. The evidence highlights the compound's involvement in signaling pathways that may influence HepG2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
